Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 9.3. Consideration of Proposals. <omitted> (c) The Company Board shall not make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change unless: (i) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with the Company’s outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, that the failure to make the Company Adverse Recommendation Change would be inconsistent with the fiduciary duties of the Company Board under applicable Law and strategic objectives of the Company, (ii) the Company has informed Parent in writing of the Company Board’s intention to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change not less than 72 hours before such change, and (iii) the decision to make a Company Adverse Recommendation Change is in connection with an Acquisition Proposal that the Company Board has determined, after consultation with its financial advisor and strategic consultants, to be a Superior Proposal. The Company shall have complied with clauses (1) through (5), as follows: (1) the Company Board shall have determined that such Acquisition Proposal is a Superior Proposal based on financial and strategic merits, (2) the Company shall have made available to Parent the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal, (3) the Company shall have negotiated in good faith with Parent to allow the Acquisition Proposal to no longer constitute a Superior Proposal, (4) after considering the results of negotiations with Parent and taking into account the proposals made by Parent, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith, after consultation with its outside legal counsel and strategic advisors, that such Acquisition Proposal remains a Superior Proposal, and (5) if the Company intends to terminate this Agreement to enter into a Specified Agreement, the Company shall have complied with Section 10.1(d)(i). For clarity, the provisions of this Section 9.3(c) shall also apply to any amendment to the financial terms or any other material amendment to any Acquisition Proposal. (Pages 85-86)\nAnswer:
